      "title": "మనవి (manavi) — a polite request",
      "headword": "మనవి",
      "romanization": "manavi",
      "gloss": "a polite request",
      "script": "telugu",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:05c47e1f4162b5d9",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: what did maryāda mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: మనవి",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "మనవి (manavi) — \"a polite request\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "మనవి (manavi) is a request made from below — not దయచేసి set in front of an instruction, but the whole thing framed as a submission. ఒక మనవి (manavi), \"one request\", is said before the request itself arrives."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Where the word came from is not something any source consulted here settles, so nothing is invented for it. What is certain is the register it sits in, and that is the part a learner needs."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A మనవి (manavi) goes to somebody who can say no: an official, an elder, a host. The word does half the softening before you have said what you want."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "manavi",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *manavi*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "it once more, slowly",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: it once more, slowly]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "manavi, then dayacēsi, and say which one is the whole request",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *manavi*, then *dayacēsi*, and say which one is the whole request]"
