    {
      "id": "TE-C65-permission",
      "sequence": 2110,
      "title": "అనుమతి (anumati) — permission",
      "headword": "అనుమతి",
      "romanization": "anumati",
      "gloss": "permission",
      "script": "telugu",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:92740fe8096e093f",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: what did manavi mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: అనుమతి",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "అనుమతి (anumati) — \"permission\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "అనుమతి (anumati) is permission — what a మనవి (manavi) is hoping to be given. అనుమతి (anumati) ఇవ్వండి, \"give permission\", is the formal shape of it; in a house it usually comes out as a nod."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It is Sanskrit: anu- \"along with\" and mati \"a mind\". Permission is somebody's mind going along with yours, which is a kinder picture than the English word offers."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Asking leave before you go is where it is most used, and it sits naturally in front of వెళ్ళొస్తాను. With అనుమతి (anumati) first, leaving stops being something you announce and becomes something you are given."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Four."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "anumati",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *anumati*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "it once more, slowly",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: it once more, slowly]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "anumati, then veḷḷostānu, and take your leave properly",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *anumati*, then *veḷḷostānu*, and take your leave properly]"
            }
          ]
        },
